      "perplexityContext": "## Key Players\n\n**Isaiah Campbell-Finch (G, Fr., 7.4 PPG)** leads the Bulldogs in scoring with 214 total points across 29 games (23.4 MPG), shooting 42.1% FG and 32.1% from three on 84 attempts; his volume scoring and 1.5 RPG make him dangerous as a quick freshman guard who exploits transition[1][4][5].  \n**Cade Norris (G, R-Sr., 9.1 PPG)** is the efficient sharpshooter at 45.9% FG and 43.5% from three (27 makes in 62 tries) over 18 starts (31.4 MPG), pairing 4.6 RPG with playmaking vision to stretch defenses[4][5].  \n**Kam Martin (G, So., 6.1 PPG)** provides bench spark with 35.3% three-point shooting (18 makes) and 1.8 APG in 32 games (17.2 MPG for 110 points), dangerous in spot-up situations and forcing turnovers (0.9 SPG)[4][5].\n\n## Team Identity\n\nSamford plays at a deliberate **tempo** (69.4 possessions, 166th nationally), emphasizing a pack-line **defensive philosophy** that forces low turnovers (11.58% defensive TO%, 352nd) while dominating offensive rebounds (25.75%, 18th)[6]. Offensively, they run a balanced scheme with strong **three-point shooting** (35.61%, 83rd) and effective FG% (53.07%, 105th), but struggle on the boards (25.28% off reb%, 333rd)[6].\n\n## Recent Form\n\nOver the last month entering the SoCon Tournament, Samford went 4-6 in their final 10 games, snapping a 3-game losing streak with a quarterfinal exit (lost to top seed, specific score unavailable); overall 13-18 regular season reflected inconsistency, finishing 11-7 in conference before bowing out early[4][7].\n\n## Strengths\n\nSamford excels at **three-point volume** (35.61% team rate) and **defensive rebounding** (25.75% OR% allowed), forcing misses and converting to transition threes; they favor matchups against slow-paced, poor-shooting teams where guards like Norris and Campbell-Finch can bomb from deep[6].\n\n## Weaknesses\n\nVulnerable on **offensive rebounding** (25.28%, 333rd) and allowing high opponent eFG% (51.86%, 207th), they struggle against athletic, fast-breaking teams that crash the glass and punish turnovers (11.96% off TO%, elite but exploitable in transition)[6].\n\n## Tournament Outlook\n\nNo reported injuries heading into the dance; first-year coach **Lennie Acuff** lacks personal NCAA Tournament experience (staff includes Tyler Murray, Vince Martin), and Samford has zero **historical March Madness wins** (0-6 all-time, last appearance 2024 as 12-seed with first-round loss)[7]. As a #16 seed with 86.5 AdjO and 98.2 AdjD, they're heavy underdogs in the Sacramento Region.\n\n## X-Factor\n\n**Cade Norris's three-point stroke** (43.5%)—if he heats up early (27 makes in 62 tries), it could keep games close against superior foes; cold nights expose their scoring depth limits[4].",
